   "source": ["---\n", "## Ejercicio 6: Async/Await Profundo\n", "\n", "**Concepto:** `async/await` permite programación asíncrona cooperativa. Ideal para I/O-bound (red, disco, BD). No bloquea el thread, permite manejar miles de conexiones simultáneas.\n", "\n", "**Ejemplo real:** Servidor web que maneja 10,000 peticiones simultáneas sin 10,000 threads."],
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["import asyncio\n", "\n", "async def fetch(url, delay):\n", "    print(f\"Iniciando {url}\")\n", "    await asyncio.sleep(delay)  # Simula I/O\n", "    print(f\"Completado {url}\")\n", "    return f\"Datos de {url}\"\n", "\n", "async def main():\n", "    # Ejecuta 3 fetches en paralelo (no secuencial)\n", "    resultados = await asyncio.gather(\n", "        fetch(\"url1\", 2),\n", "        fetch(\"url2\", 1),\n", "        fetch(\"url3\", 3),\n", "    )\n", "    print(resultados)  # 3 segundos total, no 6\n", "\n", "asyncio.run(main())"]
