   "source": ["---\n", "## Ejercicio 10: Challenge — Implementa `lru_cache` desde cero\n", "\n", "**Concepto:** `lru_cache` cachea resultados de funciones para evitar recálculos. \"LRU\" = Least Recently Used: cuando el cache está lleno, elimina el elemento menos usado recientemente.\n", "\n", "**Ejemplo real:** Cachear consultas a BD, llamadas a API, cálculos pesados en Fibonacci."],
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["from collections import OrderedDict\n", "\n", "class LRUCache:\n", "    def __init__(self, maxsize=128):\n", "        self._cache = OrderedDict()\n", "        self._maxsize = maxsize\n", "        self.hits = 0\n", "        self.misses = 0\n", "\n", "    def __call__(self, func):\n", "        from functools import wraps\n", "        @wraps(func)\n", "        def wrapper(*args):\n", "            if args in self._cache:\n", "                self._cache.move_to_end(args)\n", "                self.hits += 1\n", "                return self._cache[args]\n", "            self.misses += 1\n", "            result = func(*args)\n", "            self._cache[args] = result\n", "            if len(self._cache) > self._maxsize:\n", "                self._cache.popitem(last=False)\n", "            return result\n", "        wrapper.cache_info = lambda: {\n", "            'hits': self.hits, 'misses': self.misses,\n", "            'size': len(self._cache), 'maxsize': self._maxsize\n", "        }\n", "        return wrapper"]
  },
